  "contract": "inventory-hash-v1",
  "notes": "Per-section inventory content hash (ARCHITECTURE.md §6.1). canonical_json is exactly what the agent's Go json.Marshal emits for payload_json decoded as the agent decodes it (integers as int64, other numbers as float64); sha256 is over its UTF-8 bytes. The server must produce the same bytes from json.loads(payload_json). Go escapes < > & U+2028 U+2029, emits other non-ASCII raw, and formats floats without a trailing .0 and with exponents only outside [1e-6, 1e21). Negative zero is deliberately absent: Go emits -0, which json.loads reads as the integer 0, so parity cannot hold for it on any server encoding (collectors do not produce it).",
